# Local environment
.env
.env.local
# The machine-local half of the harness config surface: host-specific runner,
# model and policy overrides, key-merged over basicly.toml. Ignored so a
# developer's own settings never reach a commit — and because the harness
# refuses to land a worktree while the base checkout carries dirt outside
# the tracker, so an untracked one would block every landing (basicly-jr0l.7).
# Note .basicly-local/fragments/ is deliberately *tracked*: catalog overlay
# prose is shared, only this config file is per-machine.
basicly.local.toml

# Node.js
node_modules/
# package.json and package-lock.json are tracked to pin markdownlint-cli2.
# The tracker kit's derived files (basicly-vkh0.21). `.basicly/ledger/` is otherwise a
# *committed* directory — `tracker-surface.json` and `tracker-usage.jsonl` are tracked —
# so these are named individually rather than ignoring the directory: the event log that
# lands beside them is the truth and must stay tracked. An ignore rule that swallowed the
# log would delete the truth to save a cache.
#
# Both are folds of the log that anybody may delete
# (`.basicly/core/kit/tracker/snapshot.py`). Committing one recreates the dual-store
# failure the event log exists to escape: two branches each rebuild it, and a record
# changed on both sides is a same-line conflict git cannot union-merge. The patterns are
# `snapshot.DERIVED_PATTERNS`; `.scripts/kit_deployment.py` reads that tuple and fails
# naming whichever rule is missing here.
.basicly/ledger/snapshot.jsonl
.basicly/ledger/checkpoint-*.jsonl

# The worktree redirect: one line naming the checkout that owns the tracker, written at
# provisioning (`basicly.tracker_paths`). Machine-local by construction — it holds an
# absolute path — and per-worktree, so committing it would point every clone at one
# developer's checkout.
.basicly/ledger/redirect

# Session handover notes: a session's own claims about where it stopped, written
# for whoever picks up next and deleted once acted on. Local on purpose — they are
# unverified by construction, so committing them would put assertions in the repo
# beside the code that is the actual authority. Ignored for the same reason
# basicly.local.toml is: the harness refuses to land a worktree while the base
# checkout carries dirt outside the tracker, so an untracked one blocks every landing.
HANDOVER.md
